course: dictionary
lesson: 8829
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Shift is a good example: it can be a verb (to shift) or a noun (a shift). The words around it show you which meaning to use.
explain: «Help me shift this table» means move it to another place. «The wind shifted to the north» means it changed direction. «A shift is a set time at work» means a period of work. Read the words next to the word first.
explain: Test your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. If "move" makes sense, you have it. In maths, shift means to slide a shape without turning it.
fact: Shift can be a verb (shift, shifts, shifted, shifting) or a noun (a shift, shifts).
fact: «Shift» can mean to move something from one place to another, or to change.
fact: A shift is a set period of work, such as a day shift or a night shift.
fact: The shift key on a keyboard makes capital letters.
fact: In maths, a shift (also called a translation) slides a shape without turning it.
exercise: «Help me shift this table so we can sweep under it.» What does shift mean? | To count the legs | *To move something to another place | To fall asleep | To read something out loud
exercise: «The wind shifted to the north.» What does shifted mean? | Stopped completely | Blew very hard | *Changed direction | Turned into snow
exercise: «Many parents work shifts and sometimes miss shows.» What is a shift here? | A type of key | *A set period of work | A fast car | A kind of shoe
test: In maths, «shift 3 squares right» means what? | Make the shape 3 times bigger | Cut the shape into 3 pieces | Turn the shape around | *Slide the shape 3 squares to the right without turning it
test: «When a night shift runs from 22:00 to 06:00, split it in two.» How many hours is that shift in total? | *8 | 4 | 10 | 6
exam: In «the Great Vowel Shift», what does shift mean? | *A big change | Getting rid of something quickly | Moving furniture across a room | A set time at work
